 "defect_observations": [
  "Body lines 153-158 (def:p15-w02b-p15-045-conventions item 3) adopt I(1:2)=+infinity for every pair with mu_1 not << mu_2 and say this is 'justified by' thm:p15-w02b-p15-045-support, but that theorem (lines 532-545) assumes mu_2 << mu_1. The general singular-mass case is proved on the route in thm:p15-directional-log-integrability (handbook/parts/p15/robust-sequential-endpoints.tex 54-73), which the convention does not cite (the owned file cites it only at line 685). Suggest citing it at the convention or stating the one-sided restriction of the limit theorem.",
  "Body lines 614-627 (def:p15-w02b-p15-045-grouping) assert that the source's printed r=2 value .0903 is half the value of its displayed formula (0.18062). KL p.85 eq. (6.6) as opened prints .1193, .0903, .0716, 0.0, and p.86 concludes r=1 with efficiency .6007. The handbook's recomputation (r=1: 0.11928, r=2: 0.18062, J=0.19860) was checked arithmetically and agrees. Recorded only as a source-discrepancy claim for the reviewer.",
  "Body lines 686-693: the source's second-order Fisher-information expansion (2.7)-(2.9) and the general-k normal formula (2.10) are not reconstructed; only k=1 is computed (lines 432-438). No listed component requires them. Recorded for the source-extent reviewer.",
